1
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:25,980
Dan.

2
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:26,780
Come here.

3
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:28,880
Come here, hurry up.

4
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:29,760
Oh, okay.

5
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:32,860
Yes?

6
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:34,680
Is that junior handsome?

7
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:35,920
Come help me take a look, quickly.

8
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:38,040
Oh.

9
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:41,940
Do you think it'd look bad if I hit on a guy first?

10
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:44,180
Uh...

11
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:49,580
Um, didn't the faculty ask you to find the Moon representative?

12
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:52,420
Finding the Moon is for you.

13
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:54,720
But shouldn't I get to have a boyfriend too?

14
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,800
He's looking over at me!

15
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:01,420
I heard he's from your old school, isn't he?

16
00:01:01,420 --> 00:01:04,120
Aren't you going to introduce him to me?

17
00:01:04,880 --> 00:01:05,860
Uh...

18
00:01:05,860 --> 00:01:08,880
I didn't know he came to study here.

19
00:01:09,820 --> 00:01:11,300
What do you ever know anyway?

20
00:01:11,940 --> 00:01:13,720
All you do is study and go home.

21
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:14,920
Living such a super boring life.

22
00:01:15,340 --> 00:01:18,260
You should try dividing tuition fees by the number of classes, sis.

23
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:20,200
I didn't ask you to skip class, okay?

24
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:21,860
Right.

25
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:23,580
So...

26
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:26,120
Are you going to pick him as the Moon?

27
00:01:26,360 --> 00:01:27,820
Isn't he interesting?

28
00:01:27,820 --> 00:01:29,180
He's handsome, right?

29
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:31,000
Yeah.

30
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:33,260
He's so handsome!

31
00:01:33,260 --> 00:01:34,220
Hmm.

32
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:38,500
I think...

33
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:39,840
I'd better head off first, sis.

34
00:01:40,180 --> 00:01:41,280
Stay with me first.

35
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:42,380
I'll be going now.

36
00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:42,960
Are you leaving already?

37
00:01:42,960 --> 00:01:43,500
Yeah.

38
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:44,420
Leaving already?

39
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:46,240
Yes.

40
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:54,020
In the past...

41
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:04,020
Hey, how about this guy? Would he work?

42
00:03:04,440 --> 00:03:06,560
You still haven't found a Moon yet, sis?

43
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:08,700
Still haven't, obviously!

44
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:10,600
It's so hard to find.

45
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:12,160
But I think...

46
00:03:12,580 --> 00:03:14,260
that junior is quite cute.

47
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:17,340
Right? I like him too.

48
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:22,800
Excuse me.

49
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:24,960
P'Dan, do you have time to talk?

50
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:31,100
I don't know if P'Dan is free, but I certainly am!

51
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:32,560
Sit right here, sweetie.

52
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:35,840
Uh...

53
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:39,700
What's up?

54
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:42,400
Oh.

55
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:44,940
The professor recommended that I come help you with the project.

56
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:48,980
Ah, the professor mentioned it to me too.

57
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:53,260
Sure thing.

58
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:06,280
Dude, he is so handsome!

59
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:08,040
Um, P'Dan.

60
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:09,500
Yes?

61
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:12,320
Thank you.

62
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:16,060
See you around.

63
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:19,580
Sure.

64
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:22,080
So handsome!

65
00:04:23,900 --> 00:04:25,400
Yeah.

66
00:04:33,460 --> 00:04:35,020
Gosh... this math subject...

67
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:38,440
Isn't it for math tutoring?

68
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:39,580
Ah, yes it is.

69
00:04:39,580 --> 00:04:41,060
Or are we tutoring a subject on love?

70
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:43,360
Woah, no.

71
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:43,960
That's too much.

72
00:04:43,960 --> 00:04:45,800
P'Pond.

73
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:47,320
Here is the coffee you ordered, P'Pond.

74
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:48,500
Thank you very much.

75
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:50,660
And this is Matcha Latte,

76
00:04:50,660 --> 00:04:52,760
creamy milk, intense, 0% sugar,

77
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:54,120
for P'Dan.

78
00:04:55,300 --> 00:04:56,880
I didn't order this.

79
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:57,860
Oh.

80
00:04:57,860 --> 00:04:59,060
P'Pond ordered it for you.

81
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:00,680
Not overly sweet.

82
00:05:01,540 --> 00:05:02,360
Well...

83
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:04,560
I saw that you don't drink coffee,

84
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:06,800
and you seemed sleepy too. / Yeah.

85
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:08,140
You didn't get much sleep last night, did you?

86
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:10,400
Huh?

87
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:13,140
How did you know P'Dan didn't get much sleep?

88
00:05:14,580 --> 00:05:18,000
Oho! Were you secretly together last night or what?

89
00:05:21,820 --> 00:05:24,080
What do you mean "together"? No way.

90
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:27,940
I think I'll go see the professor first.

91
00:05:30,880 --> 00:05:32,900
That's it for now.

92
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:36,160
Thanks.

93
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:40,420
Hey, bro.

94
00:05:40,940 --> 00:05:41,980
Seriously speaking...

95
00:05:42,440 --> 00:05:43,840
Are you guys flirting with each other?

96
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:45,440
Crazy!

97
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:46,680
Not flirting.

98
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:48,920
We're just sitting and working together.

99
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:50,140
Really?

100
00:05:50,140 --> 00:05:53,120
But I saw P'Dan walking away blushing and squirming all the way over there.

101
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:56,680
Is that called blushing?

102
00:05:57,180 --> 00:05:58,380
Do you think...

103
00:05:58,380 --> 00:05:59,900
he was blushing because of me?

104
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:02,080
Look at that, look at that!

105
00:06:02,080 --> 00:06:05,620
You look so pleased that P'Dan blushed!

106
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:10,040
Do you think...

107
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:11,740
if I pursue him,

108
00:06:11,740 --> 00:06:12,980
would I win his heart?

109
00:06:12,980 --> 00:06:14,120
Woah.

110
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:16,120
Someone of your level shouldn't even ask me that.

111
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:18,640
You can win anyone's heart!

112
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:21,120
With a guy like him, if you go after him... let me tell you,

113
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:22,180
he won't stand a chance!

114
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:25,580
Yeah, yeah, I believe you.

115
00:06:25,580 --> 00:06:27,440
You really know how to say what I want to hear.

116
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:28,320
Well!

117
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:31,660
I'm Jamine, your biggest fan!

118
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:34,280
I know everything about you,

119
00:06:34,280 --> 00:06:37,120
and I want to be like you someday!

120
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:41,400
Haha nice! Okay I gotta go, no one is tutoring me now.

121
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:42,500
Who's gonna tutor me now?

122
00:06:42,500 --> 00:06:43,060
Eh?

123
00:06:43,440 --> 00:06:45,000
I'm heading off first.

124
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:45,700
Leaving already?

125
00:06:45,700 --> 00:06:47,420
Yeah, bye! / Huh?

126
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:18,640
Pond, why did you bring me here?

127
00:07:19,760 --> 00:07:22,320
I thought there wouldn't be anyone here.

128
00:07:24,380 --> 00:07:26,140
And also...

129
00:07:26,140 --> 00:07:28,800
I wouldn't feel so shy around you.

130
00:07:52,340 --> 00:07:53,460
Do you like it?

131
00:07:59,380 --> 00:08:00,500
I like it.

132
00:08:02,220 --> 00:08:03,460
This is a chain.

133
00:08:03,460 --> 00:08:05,440
I'm using it to chain your heart to mine.

134
00:08:55,220 --> 00:08:57,380
Thank you.

135
00:08:59,300 --> 00:09:01,700
Take good care of it.

136
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:21,920
Dan.

137
00:09:21,920 --> 00:09:22,980
Yes?

138
00:09:22,980 --> 00:09:24,460
People are saying...

139
00:09:24,460 --> 00:09:26,480
Are you dating junior Pond?

140
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:28,220
Who's "people", sis?

141
00:09:28,220 --> 00:09:29,720
The entire faculty, honey!

142
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:30,700
So, what's the deal?

143
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:33,240
You always act like you don't care about love.

144
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:36,360
If you're dating, just admit it. Don't play hard to get with me!

145
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:38,860
But seriously, Dan.

146
00:09:38,860 --> 00:09:40,700
I'm not jealous of you or anything.

147
00:09:40,980 --> 00:09:42,580
He's so handsome...

148
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:45,460
Is he really being serious with you?

149
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:47,800
I did a little digging...

150
00:09:47,800 --> 00:09:51,360
In the past, he used to act sweet with everyone, here and there.

151
00:09:52,140 --> 00:09:54,960
Is he really going to be serious with you?

152
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:56,240
If he's just playing around...

153
00:09:56,240 --> 00:09:57,780
I won't let him off easily.

154
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:02,020
Uh, well, I...

155
00:10:02,020 --> 00:10:03,960
Think carefully, my friend.

156
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:05,660
I'm just worried about you.

157
00:10:08,460 --> 00:10:10,100
Thank you.

158
00:10:10,100 --> 00:10:12,360
I'm heading off now.

159
00:10:40,660 --> 00:10:42,000
P'Dan.

160
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:43,140
Hm?

161
00:10:43,140 --> 00:10:45,100
Thank you...

162
00:10:45,100 --> 00:10:47,700
for helping me finish the project.

163
00:10:49,340 --> 00:10:50,620
Honestly...

164
00:10:50,620 --> 00:10:52,260
I'm just really talented, you know.

165
00:10:52,260 --> 00:10:53,580
So I...

166
00:10:53,580 --> 00:10:55,920
shared some of my talent with others.

167
00:10:57,220 --> 00:10:59,520
Sure, Mr. Talented.

168
00:11:01,660 --> 00:11:04,240
So when Mr. Talented looks at me like this...

169
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:06,980
Is there something you want to tell me?

170
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:10,080
Well...

171
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:14,360
A startup company contacted me.

172
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:16,060
The pay is good.

173
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:18,220
The benefits are good too.

174
00:11:18,680 --> 00:11:20,280
That's great then!

175
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:22,500
Congratulations, P'Dan!

176
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:27,840
But it's far away, Pond.

177
00:11:28,680 --> 00:11:31,300
Oh, why?

178
00:11:34,040 --> 00:11:35,720
Pond, what do you think...

179
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:38,800
you will do after you graduate?

180
00:11:39,460 --> 00:11:40,480
Hmm.

181
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:42,300
After I graduate?

182
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:43,840
I'll probably get a job.

183
00:11:43,840 --> 00:11:45,540
I want to save up a lot of money.

184
00:11:45,540 --> 00:11:47,360
I want to live in the South too.

185
00:11:47,360 --> 00:11:49,200
I want to work in the fishing industry.

186
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:51,880
I'm bored of mountains. I want to live by the sea for a change.

187
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:53,840
And what if...

188
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:56,440
you and I have to work far apart from each other?

189
00:11:57,800 --> 00:11:59,480
How would you feel, Pond?

190
00:11:59,480 --> 00:12:01,700
How should I feel?

191
00:12:01,700 --> 00:12:03,440
It's your future, P'.

192
00:12:06,020 --> 00:12:07,740
And... what about us?

193
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:10,400
Us?

194
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:12,020
I mean...

195
00:12:12,020 --> 00:12:13,820
our future.

196
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:19,200
I haven't thought about "our future" to that extent yet, P'Dan.

197
00:12:19,340 --> 00:12:22,060
I just want to graduate...

198
00:12:22,060 --> 00:12:23,500
get a job,

199
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:24,600
save money,

200
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:25,880
and move down South.

201
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:28,480
I don't want to live in the North anymore.

202
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:30,300
I want to...

203
00:12:30,300 --> 00:12:32,880
live by the sea and work in fishing.

204
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:35,520
Drive a sports car along the beach...

205
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:37,040
Man, I'd really love that!

206
00:12:40,220 --> 00:12:41,740
Oh, P'.

207
00:12:41,740 --> 00:12:42,300
Hm?

208
00:12:42,300 --> 00:12:43,780
I'll take my leave first.

209
00:12:43,780 --> 00:12:45,480
I have plans with my friends.

210
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:47,680
Got a party to catch!

211
00:12:48,480 --> 00:12:49,640
See you later, P'.

212
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:51,220
Thank you!

213
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:18,980
I didn't abandon you.

214
00:13:20,120 --> 00:13:22,460
I just chose to protect my own heart.

215
00:13:25,660 --> 00:13:27,880
I was raised well.

216
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:31,540
Why should I waste my time on someone who doesn't see me in his future?

217
00:13:35,340 --> 00:13:37,480
When you disappeared back then...

218
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:40,680
Did you think I wasn't serious about you?

219
00:13:41,100 --> 00:13:43,200
And what about my future?

220
00:13:43,200 --> 00:13:44,920
Did it really not have you in it at all?

221
00:13:45,960 --> 00:13:47,640
I'm not stupid.

222
00:13:47,640 --> 00:13:49,640
Woah, P'Dan, I WAS serious!

223
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:52,080
But you never thought about it!

224
00:13:53,260 --> 00:13:54,200
Okay!

225
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:56,000
Back then, I hadn't thought about it.

226
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,860
But after you asked me that...

227
00:13:57,860 --> 00:13:58,940
I started to think.

228
00:13:58,940 --> 00:14:00,780
I started picturing you in my future!

229
00:14:01,280 --> 00:14:02,760
But right when I started thinking about it...

230
00:14:02,760 --> 00:14:04,320
you just disappeared!

231
00:14:05,060 --> 00:14:06,440
How far did you expect me...

232
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:08,660
to think about us?

233
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:17,180
Shit!

234
00:14:21,860 --> 00:14:23,000
Okay, I'll...

235
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,160
I'll handle it myself.

236
00:14:26,460 --> 00:14:27,960
I... I'm sorry.

237
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:32,580
I'll... I'll handle it myself.

238
00:14:44,260 --> 00:14:47,040
Thanks for coming to help out.

239
00:14:47,040 --> 00:14:48,920
It's a piece of cake.

240
00:14:49,280 --> 00:14:50,560
Oh, P'Best.

241
00:14:50,560 --> 00:14:52,280
For Sis Som-O's birthday...

242
00:14:52,280 --> 00:14:54,420
Do you have a gift for her yet?

243
00:14:54,420 --> 00:14:57,900
Ah, I do. Her birthday falls on the same day as my nephew's.

244
00:14:57,900 --> 00:14:59,720
So I bought them all at once.

245
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:02,820
Sis Som's birthday is on the same day as your nephew's?

246
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:00,440
Oh!

247
00:15:02,820 --> 00:15:03,480
Yeah.

248
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:04,800
How convenient!

249
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:06,840
Oh, bro.

250
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:08,660
I wanted to tell you that...

251
00:15:08,660 --> 00:15:09,920
some of these things...

252
00:15:10,520 --> 00:15:13,180
you don't have to carry them all back.

253
00:15:13,980 --> 00:15:15,440
You can leave them here.

254
00:15:16,820 --> 00:15:18,120
Oh, it's fine.

255
00:15:18,120 --> 00:15:19,860
I'd feel bad. I'll take them all back.

256
00:15:19,860 --> 00:15:20,360
Oops.

257
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:21,540
Don't feel bad at all.

258
00:15:21,540 --> 00:15:23,720
My bedroom is like your bedroom.

259
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:25,520
You can leave anything here.

260
00:15:25,520 --> 00:15:27,240
The room is so spacious.

261
00:15:28,460 --> 00:15:30,960
It really is spacious.

262
00:15:44,800 --> 00:15:46,820
What about this picture?

263
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:55,380
Uh...

264
00:15:59,020 --> 00:16:00,040
Is this picture...

265
00:16:00,880 --> 00:16:03,700
a picture of your ex?

266
00:16:08,920 --> 00:16:10,920
Yes.

267
00:16:18,580 --> 00:16:23,080
I'll put it back where it was.

268
00:16:31,100 --> 00:16:34,260
Where should I put this belt?

269
00:16:35,100 --> 00:16:37,640
In the box is fine. Put it together with the glasses.

